 launch in the latter half of 2022.  bloomberg collaborated on this  prediction and followed up with its own  report in april also in april a linkedin  listening hinted that developer naughty  dog may be working on a remake for the  last of us the listing mentions quote qa  testing and development support plus  level point of contact for unannounced  remake project but i guess we'll have to  wait a little bit longer to find out  switching gears to a bit of weird news  call of duty warzone is currently home  to a rematch between king kong and  godzilla an operation monarch and has  discovered and banished to the not safer  work section of reddit's call of duty  war zone subreddit it is possible to hop  in a helicopter and attack kong's upper  thigh section while kong's model in war  zone isn't anatomically correct you're  technically still attacking the king's  crown jewels to efficiently farm  experience points other methods might be  easier but none are as hilarious season  3's operation monarch event ends on may  25th so let me know in the comments if  you've been enjoying it so far and what  you want from the next warzone event
 

